<p>Cala Llonga takes its name from the shape of its bay — "llonga" meaning long in Catalan — a wide, rounded inlet enclosed on both sides by pine-covered cliffs that step down toward a long stretch of sand at the water's edge. The bay's shape gives it noticeably calm, sheltered water compared with more exposed stretches of coastline elsewhere on the island, which is one of the main reasons it has developed into a popular, family-oriented resort rather than a nightlife-driven one. The beach itself runs the full width of the cove, giving even a busy summer day enough space for sunbathers, swimmers, and children playing at the shoreline without feeling crowded.</p>
